{"baseRefOid":"d4dbf28da5b6e95db8da1acfd9fecd4655821296","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUcYs_s8AAAABbCYZmw","author":{"login":"sourcery-ai"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"<!-- Generated by sourcery-ai[bot]: start review_guide -->\n\n## Reviewer's Guide\n\nThe PR fixes overlapping review-flush aggregation so follow-up callers retain all persisted/conflicted IDs and prepared-continuation evidence on both success and failure, while preserving original error identity for caller-specific failures. It adds broad deterministic, UI, and PostgreSQL-backed regression coverage and documents the audit findings and validation limits.\n\n#### Sequence diagram for preserving overlapping review-flush settlement\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Caller as Flush caller\n    participant Outbox as Review outbox\n    participant Active as Active flush\n    participant Followup as Follow-up flush\n\n    Caller->>Outbox: flushPendingReviews(maximumReviews)\n    Outbox->>Active: waitForSubmittedAttempt()\n    Active-->>Outbox: ReviewFlushResult\n    alt earlier result already settles target\n        Outbox-->>Caller: earlier ReviewFlushResult\n    else follow-up required\n        Outbox->>Followup: flushPendingReviews(...)\n        Followup-->>Outbox: later ReviewFlushResult\n        Outbox->>Outbox: combineReviewFlushResults(earlier, later)\n        Outbox-->>Caller: combined IDs and preparedContinuations\n    end\n    alt follow-up rejects with ReviewReplayError\n        Followup-->>Outbox: ReviewReplayError with flushResult\n        Outbox->>Outbox: includeEarlierFlushSettlement(earlier, later)\n        Outbox-->>Caller: caller-specific error with combined flushResult\n    end\n```\n\n### File-Level Changes\n\n| Change | Details | Files |\n| ------ | ------- | ----- |\n| Preserve complete settlement evidence when overlapping flushes trigger follow-up work or failures. | <ul><li>Added shared result-merging logic for persisted IDs, conflicted IDs, and prepared continuations.</li><li>Applied the merge to bounded-to-unlimited and submitted-attempt follow-up branches.</li><li>Created caller-specific replay errors on follow-up failure while retaining the original error metadata and leaving shared observers unchanged.</li></ul> | `app/lib/review-outbox.ts` |\n| Add deterministic regression coverage for overlapping flush attribution, evidence retention, and authorization safety. | <ul><li>Covered successful and failed follow-ups, continuation-map retention, error identity, duplicate observers, explicit retry attribution, receipt recovery, conflicts, ordering, and generation boundaries.</li><li>Added Home, prepared-continuation, and pending-review recovery scenarios validating that retained evidence cannot cause duplicate or invalid advancement.</li></ul> | `tests/unit/review-outbox-regressions.test.ts`<br/>`tests/unit/prepared-review-continuation-regressions.test.ts`<br/>`tests/unit/review-attempt-confirmation-regressions.test.tsx`<br/>`tests/unit/pending-review-recovery-regressions.test.tsx`<br/>`tests/REGRESSIONS.md` |\n| Extend browser coverage to validate real persistence and reconnect overlap behavior. | <ul><li>Added a PostgreSQL-backed workflow that holds review confirmation, triggers reconnect-driven overlap, verifies one durable review and issued-successor handling, then exercises restart and replay cleanup.</li></ul> | `tests/browser/post-review-progression.spec.ts` |\n| Document the independently audited defect, correction boundaries, and validation evidence. | <ul><li>Recorded the two confirmed evidence-loss modes and explicitly distinguished settlement evidence from persistence authorization.</li><li>Documented generation-observation findings, scenario coverage, test commands, limitations, and retained durability-test failures.</li></ul> | `docs/review-outbox-settlement-audit.md` |\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Tips and commands</summary>\n\n#### Interacting with Sourcery\n\n- **Trigger a new review:** Comment `@sourcery-ai review` on the pull request.\n- **Continue discussions:** Reply directly to Sourcery's review comments.\n- **Generate a GitHub issue from a review comment:** Ask Sourcery to create an\n  issue from a review comment by replying to it. You can also reply to a\n  review comment with `@sourcery-ai issue` to create an issue from it.\n- **Generate a pull request title:** Write `@sourcery-ai` anywhere in the pull\n  request title to generate a title at any time. You can also comment\n  `@sourcery-ai title` on the pull request to (re-)generate the title at any time.\n- **Generate a pull request summary:** Write `@sourcery-ai summary` anywhere in\n  the pull request body to generate a PR summary at any time exactly where you\n  want it. You can also comment `@sourcery-ai summary` on the pull request to\n  (re-)generate the summary at any time.\n- **Generate reviewer's guide:** Comment `@sourcery-ai guide` on the pull\n  request to (re-)generate the reviewer's guide at any time.\n- **Resolve all Sourcery comments:** Comment `@sourcery-ai resolve` on the\n  pull request to resolve all Sourcery comments. Useful if you've already\n  addressed all the comments and don't want to see them anymore.\n- **Dismiss all Sourcery reviews:** Comment `@sourcery-ai dismiss` on the pull\n  request to dismiss all existing Sourcery reviews. Especially useful if you\n  want to start fresh with a new review - don't forget to comment\n  `@sourcery-ai review` to trigger a new review!\n\n#### Customizing Your Experience\n\nAccess your [dashboard](https://app.sourcery.ai) to:\n- Enable or disable review features such as the Sourcery-generated pull request\n  summary, the reviewer's guide, and others.\n- Change the review language.\n- Add, remove or edit custom review instructions.\n- Adjust other review settings.\n\n#### Getting Help\n\n- [Contact our support team](mailto:support@sourcery.ai) for questions or feedback.\n- Visit our [documentation](https://docs.sourcery.ai) for detailed guides and informa